WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.128 --> 00:00:05.005
Welcome to Tokyo.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.184
I'm here.

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:19.894
And?

00:00:20.103 --> 00:00:21.479
And what, Mom?

00:00:22.063 --> 00:00:25.066
You think he'll just be sitting here,
waiting for someone to bring him home?

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:29.279
Who are you?

00:00:29.904 --> 00:00:30.447
What are you doing here?

00:00:30.447 --> 00:00:31.573
- Who are you?
- What do you want?

00:00:31.573 --> 00:00:32.073
- Who are you?
- What do you want?

00:00:33.408 --> 00:00:34.159
What are you doing?

00:00:34.576 --> 00:00:36.411
This is my father.

00:00:38.913 --> 00:00:39.831
What do you want?

00:00:39.831 --> 00:00:42.959
Can you tell us anything?

00:00:43.668 --> 00:00:45.503
We have been waiting.

00:00:45.587 --> 00:00:47.088
Let's just forget this happened.

00:00:47.464 --> 00:00:48.381
Are you kidding me?

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:50.759
You flew halfway around the world
looking for something.

00:00:50.759 --> 00:00:53.136
And all you found was Dad was apparently
a lying a**hole.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:55.055
I want to show you something.

00:00:55.638 --> 00:00:57.057
He just wasn’t who you say he was.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.391
Got to give it to the guy.

00:00:58.975 --> 00:01:01.811
He had two families and still had time
to be obsessed with work.

00:01:02.604 --> 00:01:03.438
It was important.

00:01:03.438 --> 00:01:04.856
Do you even know what he did?

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:06.232
Woah, hey!

00:01:08.109 --> 00:01:09.027
What's in here?

00:01:09.027 --> 00:01:10.195
I didn't know it was there.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:26.211
They were there.

00:01:26.211 --> 00:01:27.587
In San Francisco.

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:31.549
Like soldiers or something.
With this on their uniforms.

00:01:31.549 --> 00:01:33.510
You think that your father was working for them?

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.011
This stuff was in his safe.

00:01:35.011 --> 00:01:37.263
She wants to know if he was with you.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:39.307
When it happened, was he with you?

00:01:39.724 --> 00:01:41.267
What difference does that make now?

00:01:41.351 --> 00:01:42.519
You don't think it would've
made a difference

00:01:42.519 --> 00:01:44.187
if he'd been here with us instead?

00:01:44.187 --> 00:01:46.106
No, he wasn’t with me.

00:01:54.072 --> 00:01:58.451
About a week after that, we got a call
from the state police in Fairbanks, Alaska

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:00.912
saying the bush plane he was on
disappeared in a storm.

00:02:00.912 --> 00:02:02.956
They never found the wreckage.

00:02:02.956 --> 00:02:04.624
What are you all going to do now?

00:02:04.624 --> 00:02:06.793
“You can do this.”

00:02:06.793 --> 00:02:08.503
“I believe in you.”

00:02:08.503 --> 00:02:09.963
That’s what you said that time.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:12.465
But I didn’t want to disappoint you.

00:02:13.216 --> 00:02:14.717
So I couldn’t face you...

00:02:14.717 --> 00:02:17.220
How was I supposed to know
I’d never see you again?

00:02:33.528 --> 00:02:34.821
Colonel Shaw?

00:02:37.198 --> 00:02:39.117
We want to find out what
happened to my father.

00:02:39.117 --> 00:02:41.578
Now you can choke down that
mountain of Monarch bullsh*t

00:02:41.578 --> 00:02:43.997
about your father disappearing
without a trace.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.958
Or, we can get the hell out of here
right now and find out

00:02:46.958 --> 00:02:48.585
what really happened with your dad.

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:51.212
Did our dad really work for them?
For Monarch?

00:02:51.212 --> 00:02:51.254
Did our dad really work for them?
For Monarch?

00:02:51.254 --> 00:02:53.298
It is your family business.

00:02:53.298 --> 00:02:54.674
It's not our family business…

00:02:55.508 --> 00:02:56.801
it's the family curse.

00:03:01.598 --> 00:03:03.016
Go! Run!

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:04.100
May!

00:03:07.145 --> 00:03:08.563
May, come on!

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:11.274
I got you!

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:13.526
Come on, hurry!

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.903
Kentaro!
-Let’s go!

00:03:14.903 --> 00:03:16.029
Kentaro?
-We’re going to go.

00:03:16.029 --> 00:03:16.529
Go!

00:03:16.905 --> 00:03:17.697
Go!

00:03:26.247 --> 00:03:29.584
They said the signal was so weak, they almost didn’t
hear me on the emergency channel.

00:03:29.584 --> 00:03:33.087
I never thought I’d thank someone for
abandoning their family but

00:03:33.546 --> 00:03:34.339
here we are.

00:03:34.339 --> 00:03:37.008
He'd scribble down
every crazy thing he came across

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:39.344
till his pencils were nothing but nubs.

00:03:39.344 --> 00:03:40.637
- Dad did that.
- Yeah?

00:03:40.637 --> 00:03:42.639
He'd sharpen them
with the penknife that he carried.

00:03:42.931 --> 00:03:44.682
Left the shavings everywhere.

00:03:44.974 --> 00:03:46.559
I know that handwriting.

00:03:47.185 --> 00:03:48.186
Me too.

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.439
He survived.

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:01.074
Monarch may know how to find the Titans,
but they don't know how to find Dad.

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:03.910
Do we? I already searched his office an--

00:04:03.993 --> 00:04:05.286
Not the one in San Francisco.

00:04:05.828 --> 00:04:07.789
Dad would sing these cheesy commercials.

00:04:10.124 --> 00:04:12.210
What is the secret of the triangle shape?

00:04:14.128 --> 00:04:16.714
The secret of deliciousness is...

00:04:16.798 --> 00:04:18.216
I'm not going to tell you!

00:04:18.216 --> 00:04:18.758
Tada!

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:20.760
San Francisco.

00:04:21.844 --> 00:04:23.346
Alaska.

00:04:27.392 --> 00:04:27.892
Africa.

00:04:28.101 --> 00:04:29.352
This must be the path he took.

00:04:30.478 --> 00:04:31.521
Is that--

00:04:42.824 --> 00:04:43.825
He's alive.

00:04:45.201 --> 00:04:49.747
Dad! Over here, Dad!

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:53.876
-Dad!
-Up here!

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:54.752
Dad!

00:05:05.221 --> 00:05:07.307
We gotta get out of here!
Come on, we gotta move! Now!

00:05:07.390 --> 00:05:09.559
Now! Move! We need to go now!

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:10.727
Kentaro, we gotta go!

